<%--
    CSRF token bootstrap for JSPs that do AJAX POSTs reading
    document.querySelector('input[name="CSRF-TOKEN"]').

    Why: CSRFGuard's client script only injects the hidden CSRF-TOKEN
    input into <form> elements whose action attribute is a valid URL and
    whose method is non-GET. JSPs without such a form (e.g. pages that
    only use action="javascript:void(0)" forms, action-less forms, or no
    forms at all) will silently fail every POST. Including this fragment
    populates the token via share/javascript/csrfTokenFetch.js.

    Usage — place the include anywhere inside <body>, once per page:
        <%@ include file="/WEB-INF/jspf/csrf-token.jspf" %>

    Notes:
      * fetchCsrfToken(contextPath) returns a Promise that resolves after
        the token is populated and rejects on fetch/parse failure. Callers
        that trigger AJAX POSTs immediately on page load should await
        resolution or handle rejection rather than relying on the fire-
        and-forget DOMContentLoaded bootstrap below.
      * The bootstrap's promise is published as window.csrfTokenReady so a
        handler firing before it settles can await it instead of reading a
        still-empty input. It is null until DOMContentLoaded, and rejects if
        the fetch failed, so callers must handle both: `if (ready) await
        ready` inside a try/catch, then re-check the input. A rejection
        handler is attached here purely to keep an unawaited failure from
        surfacing as an unhandled rejection; awaiting callers still see it.
      * Include this fragment exactly once per page — duplicate includes
        load csrfTokenFetch.js twice and register two DOMContentLoaded
        handlers (idempotent, but wasteful).
      * Content-Security-Policy: the bootstrap below is an INLINE script, so
        a page that sets a script-src without 'unsafe-inline' silently gets
        no CSRF token and every save fails with an error the user never
        sees. Such a page must generate a nonce, put 'nonce-<value>' in its
        own script-src, and expose the same value as the "cspNonce" request
        attribute BEFORE this include. The nonce attribute is then emitted
        here; pages that set no attribute are unaffected.
--%>
<%@ taglib uri="carlos" prefix="carlos" %>
<script type="text/javascript"
        src="${carlos:forHtmlAttribute(pageContext.request.contextPath)}/share/javascript/csrfTokenFetch.js"></script>
<input type="hidden" name="CSRF-TOKEN" value="">
<%-- Emitted only when the including page published a nonce; otherwise absent, as before. --%>
<script<%= request.getAttribute("cspNonce") == null ? ""
        : " nonce=\"" + io.github.carlos_emr.carlos.utility.SafeEncode.forHtmlAttribute(
                String.valueOf(request.getAttribute("cspNonce"))) + "\"" %>>
    window.csrfTokenReady = null;
    document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", function () {
        window.csrfTokenReady =
            fetchCsrfToken('${carlos:forJavaScript(pageContext.request.contextPath)}');
        window.csrfTokenReady.catch(function () { /* awaiting callers handle it */ });
    });
</script>
